  "quantity": "low-backscatter area (HH)",
  "terminology": "The quantity reported is low-backscatter area (HH), defined strictly as the surface area of pixels whose HH radar backscatter is below a given decibel threshold. It is NOT termed \"water area\" because at L-band, backscatter below moderate thresholds (-16 dB to -10 dB) encompasses wet agricultural fields, inundated vegetation, and saturated wetlands in addition to open water bodies. Only values below -20 dB are primarily specular water surfaces.",
